  ],
  "text": "You are not seeing the world. You are seeing your brain's best guess about it. There is a hole in each of your eyes where the nerve leaves. No light lands there at all. You have never noticed it, because your brain fills the gap with whatever is nearby. It is not leaving it blank. It invents the missing patch and hands it to you as fact. Colour works the same way. Your brain corrects for the light in the room before you see anything. Which is why one grey square can look like two different greys in the same picture. And vision is slow. The signal takes real time to arrive. So your brain does not show you now. It predicts where things will be and shows you that. Illusions are not glitches. They are that prediction system caught showing its working. Everything you have ever seen was a guess that happened to be good enough. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
